  "name": "transcript: speculative capture can clobber a just-written transcript_ref and mutates transcripts on failed commands",
  "slug": "transcript-speculative-capture-can",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "transcript: speculative capture can clobber a just-written transcript_ref and mutates transcripts on failed commands",
    "details_md": "resolveTranscriptCapture compares only session id (transcript.ts:903-911), so a concurrent review --transcript + done race lets done write transcript_ref:null over the fresh ref. Also speculative capture runs BEFORE state validation (stop.ts:65), so a stop on a review-state ticket overwrites the captured transcript bytes then exits CONFLICT — audit artifact changed with no event.",
    "acceptance": [
      "reconciliation also compares transcript_ref (re-run keep-existing branch in-lock)",
      "speculative capture never overwrites when the command then fails validation"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/sessions/transcript.ts:903",
      "src/cli/commands/stop.ts:65"
    ],
